ArtemisOS modifications: process-local root bootstrap and parent lifetime watch;
retain root only in the dedicated display server; request a secure auto-mirrored
default display and a secure-only compatibility fallback; rebuild scripts and
focused policy regression tests. The official Windows C client is unchanged.

This is a modified server, not an official upstream release. The wire protocol
version remains 4.1 for compatibility with the unmodified official client.
Android framework AIDL/hidden-interface stub notices are retained in the complete
upstream source archive. Other redistributed client dependencies keep their
existing separate licenses and source notices.
